# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the CI `tsan: true` leg.
#
# UniFFI's generated async bridge (`uniffiRustCallAsync` in livekit_uniffi.swift) parks a Swift
# task in `withUnsafeContinuation` and lets a Rust thread resume it from
# `uniffiFutureContinuationCallback`. TSan reports the resuming thread's read of the task frame
# against the resumed task's first write to it as a race: it cannot see the happens-before edge
# the Swift runtime's continuation handoff provides, because the resuming thread is a Rust
# (tokio) thread it has no Swift-concurrency instrumentation for. The code is generated by
# uniffi-rs and shipped in the LiveKitUniFFI xcframework, so it cannot be changed here; a report
# aborts the whole test host, which has failed an otherwise green macOS TSan leg mid-suite
# (during `DataTrackStressTests.concurrentPush`).
#
# Scoped to that one callback so anything else TSan finds still fails the leg.
race:*uniffiFutureContinuationCallback*
